There’s also a version by The Seekers.

TIP:  The opening three notes (untransposed - notes may or many not transpose) are top string/3rd fret, open 5th string, and 5th string/2nd fret.  Then pick the 5th string and strum (C/G) followed by the top string and strum (C/G).  Repeat.  

TIP:  Assuming it even has one and it’s not just a musical convenience, the most accepted, albeit speculative, Gaelic meaning attributed to the chorus is “musha ringum du dum da” means “whiskey for the fool” and “whack fall the daddy-o” is “in memory of my father.”  
   

